<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brielle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Den Briel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brielle is a small fortified town in South Holland near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Maas</a>, known in English as Brill. On 1 April 1572 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-beggars">Sea Beggars</a>, Calvinist privateers recently expelled from English ports, captured it from the Spanish, giving the rebels their first foothold in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. The capture set off revolts across Holland and Zeeland and is still commemorated in the town each year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brielle.jpg" alt="Brielle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Debot at Dutch Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brielle_vesting_20050518.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
